  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provide Based Needs Protection and Medical Assistance to the Yemenis Affected Populations, Returnees, and Migrants in Yemen Yemen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Due to the escalation of violent events and the constant shifts in fighting along frontlines between the conflicting parties, Yemen has plunged into one of the most severe and large-scale humanitarian crises presently experienced in the world. With over three years since the conflict escalated, Yemenis are still struggling with the deterioration of economic situation; the already precarious humanitarian situation has continued to deteriorate as a result of damage to civilian infrastructure and the disruption of what were already threadbare basic services. 
 
The proposed intervention is geared to contribute to the strengthening of capacities, awareness, and direct assistance for a greater protection and wellbeing of the most vulnerable conflict-affected populations in Yemen and to the Yemeni returnees from aboard. Through this intervention, IOM is planning to implement a series of actions aimed at reducing suffering, mortality, and morbidity among communities.</narrative>
  </description>
